---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DebtPayoffCalculator from '../../components/DebtPayoffCalculator';
---

<Layout
  title="Debt Payoff Calculator"
  description="Free debt payoff calculator. Compare the snowball and avalanche methods side by side to see which pays off your debts faster and cheaper."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand">Tool<span class="text-orange">/</span></p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-paper sm:text-4xl">Debt Payoff Calculator</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted">
      Enter your debts and see how the snowball and avalanche payoff methods compare, side by side.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <DebtPayoffCalculator client:load />
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-10 max-w-none prose-a:text-brand">
      <h2>How this calculator works</h2>
      <p>
        This tool simulates paying down your debts month by month under two strategies: the <strong>avalanche
        method</strong> (extra payments go to the highest-interest debt first) and the <strong>snowball
        method</strong> (extra payments go to the smallest balance first). As each debt is paid off, its minimum
        payment is rolled into the next target debt under both methods.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read our full <a href="/blog/debt-payoff-snowball-vs-avalanche/">debt snowball vs. avalanche guide</a> for
        the reasoning behind each approach and which might fit you better.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
